From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:18:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: apple-sftl: Follow native allocation and checkpoint
 accounting order

Allocate a fresh context group and verify the previous occupied site
independently of the new base list. Preserve cached scalar statistics
during a save, sample the VFL and PPN after the base page, and reconcile
successful releases and wear before granting reuse to the normal writer.

Model healthy free-block selection and clean-pool maintenance. Inspect
unlisted context-role blocks during recovery and fail closed on ambiguous
torn records. Cover disjoint groups, interrupted saves, missing counter
history, completion failures and wear boundaries on synthetic NAND.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/226#issuecomment-7133476475
---
